WasmFS: every backend failure to create a symlink is reported as EPERM

Directory::insertSymlink() could only return null, so symlink() turned
every backend failure into EPERM. It now returns a MaybeFile, which
carries a negative error code; the Node backend reports the host's
(EACCES, EROFS, ENOSPC, ...), the OPFS backend, which has no symlinks,
says EPERM itself, and inserting into an unlinked directory is ENOENT.
Backends that still return plain null get EPERM, as before.

Upstream: not filed yet
Draft: docs/upstream/emscripten-wasmfs-symlink-errors.md

